how do you juggle your time if you're  like most entrepreneurs you're working  crazy hours putting everything you got  into your business running every  position in your business from the CEO  down to the janitor and if you really  want to have breakthroughs then you have  to make sure you're spending your time  wisely because that's the biggest asset  that's going into your company and if  you spend too much time on the wrong  project it could sink your business so  got a question from an entrepreneur love  more who wrote in to say how do you  juggle your time and the running of your  business empire so I could go on for a  long time talking about time management  all the different stuff that I've done  but a few highlights that may help guide  your thinking if you think about how  you're going to spend your time the  first thing you need to think about is  eliminating the things that you don't  need to do too many of us are running  programs and projects and initiatives  that we do not need to do they are not  really adding much to our business you  could eliminate a lot of the stuff on  your plate right now and it would have  zero impact on your bottom line the next  thing is look at what you can automate I  hate doing the same thing over and over  and over and over again first of all  you're likely to make mistakes second of  all it's really boring and third of all  it's not a good use of your time if  anything can be automated things should  find ways to do it and look at software  that can help you or create your own  software or web tools to help you do it  a great example is accounting right if  you're doing accounting and you're using  Excel you're you know have your receipts  in a shoebox just get an account in  software package it's so much faster it  saves you so much time I just download  my statements pop it into my counter  software remembers everything and spits  out the statement and it takes for like  20 minutes a quarter to do my account  super simple because most of it is  automated I have a programmer on staff  and he will help take a lot of the  things that I hate doing repeatedly you  have to do something two or three times  then I try to find a way to automate it  because I'm going to start making  mistakes I get bored and there's better  use  my time the third thing to think about  is delegation so we've eliminated all  the stuff we shouldn't be doing we've  automated as much as possible then look  at what's left on your plate so these  are mission critical things things are  really helping grow your business you  don't have to do everything yourself you  got to think about what are you best at  in the world and how can you delegate  the other things away to other people  people usually start delegating admin  stuff right nobody likes to an admin  stuff entrepreneurs hate doing admin  work we like the big picture we like the  visionary stuff we like the exciting  projects it's never the admitted me so I  could spend that hour doing something  else right you don't have to hire a  full-time person straight off the bat  but doing those things quickly frees up  your time to focus on the higher  priority projects a few more tips that  will help you I've got a lot to say on  this stuff so if you want more detail  anything particular let me know because  I've created a whole sections of  worksheets on this and you can go  through to help figure this out for you  better so some more ideas one I don't  answer my phone my phone number is not  on my business card and if somebody  calls in I don't pick it up unless it's  my family because they know my number  most people don't even know my number  when the phone rings in my office is a  surprise like who's calling because  phone calls are such a waste of time  unscheduled phone calls I do a lot of  business by the phone but I'm always  calling out the people at set times  because when somebody calls you up  you're in the middle of working on  something what happens the answer the  phone may even take five minutes you put  down the phone you figure out what you  were doing it takes you half an hour  just to get back in the flow of where  you were before unscheduled phone calls  are other people's agenda for your time  and you can't let them take up your time  okay next e-mails can be the same thing  right the email comes in if you check  every minute it comes in ding ding the  light goes off you stop working on what  you're doing to check your email huge  productivity suck either check your  email at a designated time spend an hour  a day doing email and then let it go or  sort it at least you have really  important people we  we'll check frequently and everybody  else can wait until the next day next  try to build a no crisis business I hate  working with clients who are I don't  want to say demanding but always in a  state of emergency like we need this  right now we need this right now so  you're constantly just reacting and  putting out fires instead of proactively  growing and building your business so I  work with clients who respect my process  and who I can deliver great results to  if they follow the process I'm just  working on a deal with a huge company in  the US and then kind of under NDA so I  can't say anything with the name but  they wanted me to sign a contract like  sure I'll signed the contract no problem  send me send me the contract up but they  wouldn't do it electronically they FedEx  it to me and wanted me to then FedEx it  back to them one page to be fed ex that  I could scan in easily send it off and  it took me a long time they took me like  two weeks to do it because i never could  go down the street to my fedex office to  do it because i was so busy doing other  stuff it wasn't important enough for me  to go and spend that time doing this  could be a big contract for me and so  today i actually made it to the office  send it out and just as I was I was  finishing the guy emailed me and said  hey what's happening with the contract  that we still on and I robot to say I  just sent it out today here's a tracking  number if you sent this electronically  it would have been done the next day I  love econ tracks and a little happy face  and sand and I said okay okay well know  that for next time and so it's training  people to respect your time and your  process because if the companies that I  work with always made me do that stuff I  just be running around with my head cut  off never actually being able to do  anything to grow my business so those  are a few tips for you I still got a ton  the same time management but I'm you  know conscious of your your time  watching YouTube video if you liked the  video you want to see more please give  it a thumbs up below and if you have  further questions you want going to dive  deeper on any of these topics or you  have a different question for your  business leave  below in the comments and I'll  absolutely create a video response for  you thank you so much and I'll see you  soon
 

